[summary:string]
A guest appearance on the *Dynamic Devs* podcast (episode 158), where host Jonathan González and I talked about DevRel, developer communities, and the people behind the technologies we use—and how those communities end up shaping products, adoption, and the way companies relate to developers.

[duration:string]
Aug 19, 2026

[place_url:string]
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ap3DQPEzkk0

[place:string]
Remote

[content:md]
I joined **Jonathan González** on the *Dynamic Devs* podcast for episode 158, "La tecnología también se construye en comunidad" (Technology is also built in community).

### Developers decide what to trust
Companies build technology, but it's developers who decide what to trust and what to adopt. We talked about what that means for DevRel: the role isn't to push a product, it's to earn the credibility that makes developers want to use it in the first place.

### The people behind the tech
We dug into the human side of Developer Relations—the people behind the tools and platforms we use every day—and why that human layer matters as much as the technology itself.

### How community shapes the product
We also explored how developer communities feed back into the product itself, influence adoption, and change the way companies end up relating to the developers they're trying to reach.

